{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjFt81jGaW3bnQWus5Q9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HLty8cBMMNfTnRpftFiDo1","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"working":"Start: a G#5 8th above the staff, then an 8th rest, then 'pianis:' with four 16ths E5 D#5 C#5 B4. That is the end of bar 24 (G#5 8th, rest, pp E5 D#5 C#5 B4). Next bar: A4, A4 G#4, F#4 G#4, A4 F#4 = bar 25. Next: G#4 E4, G#5 with trill, A5 B5 = bar 26. Next: B5 with trill, C#5 dotted, C#5, C#5 with trill, A5 F#5 = bar 27. Next: D#5 B4, E5 D#5 C#5 B4 = bar 28. Next: the same figure as bar 25 = bar 29. Next: G#4 E4, then 'poco for.' and 32nds rising to B5 and falling = bar 30. Next: 32nds C#5 D#5 E5 D#5, E5 A4, B4 8th, B4 B4, marked 'pianis:' = bar 31. The last bar has an E4 8th with a staccato dot, an 8th rest with a fermata above, and then the double bar. That is the first half of bar 32, up to the repeat sign inside that bar. The pp G4 16ths after the repeat are on the next line. So the line holds bars 24 to 32, not 24 to 31.","right":false,"insights":"Most bars were easy to match, because bars 25 and 29 repeat and bar 30 has a distinctive run of 32nds. The error is at the end. The line closes with a partial bar: only the E4 and the rest with a fermata, before the repeat double bar that falls inside bar 32. Matching would have been easier if the edition's text marked where the repeat falls inside bar 32, for example 'E4 8th, rest 8th fermata | repeat | pp G4...'. Then it would be clear that this short final bar is the first half of bar 32."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5767,"cache_read_input_tokens":523,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5767},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":